counterfactuals.output:
A method performed by a user equipment (UE), the method comprising:

receiving, at a General Packet Radio Service mobility management/session management (GMM/SM) layer of the UE, an authentication and key agreement (AKA) request from a serving General Packet Radio Service support node (SGSN);

identifying an algorithm selected for processing the AKA request;

deriving a cryptographic key based at least in part on the selected algorithm;

verifying a message authentication code (MAC) associated with the AKA request using the derived cryptographic key; and

in response to successful verification of the MAC, generating an authenticated AKA response and transmitting the authenticated AKA response to the SGSN.
